, "move": "pass", "lead_before": -21.78, "lead_after": -22.0, "points_lost": -0.22, "best": "E7"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Crawling Along the Seventh Line", "summary": "The 20k won as White by 22 points. The game was close early, with GPT-6.1 Sol's lead between -0.1 and -4.0 through the first twelve moves. The turn came on the left side, where GPT-6.1 Sol's moves at B7, A7 and C4 lost 7.0, 11.8 and 10.1 points. The 20k also gave back 7.9 and 10.9 points with B8 and A8, but the deficit never closed, and the game ended with two passes at around -22 for Black.", "moments": [{"turn": 13, "text": "C7 lost 3.8 points, dropping Black's lead from -3.0 to -6.8, and it was the first real slide. The engine preferred G4, and the stones pushed up the left side while the centre and right stayed open."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "B7 extended the row along the seventh line and lost 7.0 points, from -6.3 to -13.3. It was a lot to pay for a move that only crept sideways beside White's C8 stone."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "A7 was the worst move of Black's game, losing 11.8 points and taking the lead from -5.3 to -17.2. It left three Black stones in a row on the seventh line, with White's row on the eighth sitting right above them."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "The 20k answered with A8, which lost 10.9 points, taking the score from -17.2 back to -6.3. White's B8 the move before had also lost 7.9, so the edge crawl was a swap of gifts, and Black got the better of this one."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "Black could not use the reprieve, and C4 lost 10.1 points, sending the score from -6.3 to -16.4. The engine wanted G4, on the open right side. The game never came back within 13 points after this."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script either called the go tools (choose_opponent, play, board), read or wrote notes and logs, or ran the inspect73 flood-fill (groups, liberties, empty regions, displayed area) and the verification replay of the actual mo